WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.876
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 8: Wonderful Water.

2
00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:12.854
In this unit you will learn about water — where it comes
from, where we find it, and all the ways we use it every day.

3
00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:17.875
You will meet rainy and sunny
weather, animals that live in water,

4
00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:22.440
and the big idea that water is a gift we should never waste.

5
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:30.657
Say the words out loud — this is about confident English
and being thankful for water, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:37.048
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:45.073
By the end of this unit, you will be able to say
why plants, animals, and people all need water.

8
00:00:45.153 --> 00:00:51.008
You will also name places where we
find water (rain, river, sea, well).

9
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:57.110
You will also say how we use water:
“I use water to drink / wash / cook.”

10
00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.203
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:05.521
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: water, rain, drop, wet, dry, clean.

12
00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:10.838
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

13
00:01:10.918 --> 00:01:14.974
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

14
00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:20.072
The reading sequence includes The Well in
the Village and Talk about Wonderful Water.

15
00:01:20.152 --> 00:01:20.911
Read actively.

16
00:01:20.991 --> 00:01:25.049
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

17
00:01:25.129 --> 00:01:28.947
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

18
00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:32.833
The first language focus is Say what you use water for.

19
00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:35.729
Think of one way you use water every day.

20
00:01:35.809 --> 00:01:38.414
After 'to', use the plain action word.

21
00:01:38.494 --> 00:01:46.114
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

22
00:01:46.194 --> 00:01:50.103
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:54.484
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

24
00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:57.819
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

25
00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:01.284
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

26
00:02:01.364 --> 00:02:02.853
You are ready to begin.

27
00:02:02.933 --> 00:02:09.604
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

28
00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:12.878
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

29
00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:20.447
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
